# Previous Talks Are Read-Only Archives

The `defense/previous_talks/` directory contains **archived Beamer slide decks** from prior conference presentations (ASE, REP). Treat every path under `defense/previous_talks/` as **read-only** in this repository.

## Required behavior

- **Do not modify** any file under `defense/previous_talks/` (`.tex`, `.sty`, figures, build artifacts, scripts, etc.).
- **You may read freely** any source file when drafting the thesis defense slides (`defense/slides.tex`): slide wording, figure paths, numerical macros, and narrative structure are useful reference material.
- **Prefer LaTeX sources over PDFs** when reusing content: grep `short.tex` and `numbers.tex` rather than extracting text from rendered PDFs.
- When adapting prior material, **edit `defense/slides.tex`** (and its `defense/` assets) — never edit the archived decks in place.

If a task requires changing an archived talk, stop and tell the user to edit the upstream project or copy the deck out of `previous_talks/` first.

## Current inventory

### `defense/previous_talks/ASE_talk/` (ASE — altered git histories)

Beamer deck for the altered-histories paper. Key files:

- `short.tex` — slide entry point
- `numbers.tex` — numerical macros
- `figs/` — talk figures (classification, SWH diagrams, distributions)
- `feedback.md` — presentation feedback notes
- `short.pdf`, `research-1797-slides*.pdf` — rendered exports

### `defense/previous_talks/REP_talk/` (ACM REP 2026 — git tag alterations)

Beamer deck for the tag-alterations paper. Key files:

- `short.tex` — slide entry point
- `numbers.tex` — numerical macros
- `figs/` — talk figures (taxonomy, temporal evolution, popularity, SWH snapshots)
- `beamerthemetptng.sty` — shared beamer theme (also present in ASE_talk)
- `short.pdf` — rendered export

New archived talks may appear under `defense/previous_talks/` over time; the same read-only rule applies to all of them.
